@startuml sca-status
' scaStatus — the vocabulary SRC-IG §14.16 fixes, as INV-AUT-01 constrains it.
' PROPOSAL generated by AI. Mapped onto the two surfaces SRC-ADR names.
title scaStatus (SRC-IG §14.16) — INV-AUT-01

[*] --> received : authorisation sub-resource created
received --> psuIdentified : PSU identified
psuIdentified --> psuAuthenticated : CIAM login screen passed
psuAuthenticated --> scaMethodSelected : OTP, QR code or biometrics chosen
scaMethodSelected --> started : the enrolled device is asked
started --> unconfirmed : SCA done, confirmation call still due (Q-29)
started --> finalised : confirmed on the device, digest matches
unconfirmed --> finalised : confirmation call received
started --> failed : rejected on the device, or the digest does not match
psuAuthenticated --> failed : SCA window closed (Q-24)
received --> exempted : SCA exemption applied (Q-27)
finalised --> [*]
failed --> [*]
exempted --> [*]

note right of scaMethodSelected
  Browser: SCR-CIAM-LOGIN.
  Device: SCR-APP-OTP, SCR-APP-QR,
  SCR-APP-BIOMETRIC, then for a consent
  SCR-APP-CONSENT-CONFIRM.
end note

note bottom
  unconfirmed exists only if the bank requires the §7.6
  confirmation call, which is undecided (Q-29).
  exempted is drawn because the code list has it; whether
  the bank applies exemptions is Q-27.
end note
@enduml
